{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>None calls with justice.</b> A rebuke." "<b>And none is judged.</b> An attribute of the noun." "<b>Trusting in emptiness.</b> That a man says to his fellow, 'Thus I will do,' and he does not fulfill his word." "<b>They conceive trouble.</b> A metaphor for thought." "<b>And give birth.</b> And that is speech."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 59, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:11.920730279Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}